## stairs-power

stairs-power-ask = What power do you develop running up the stairs?
stairs-power-title = Work and power: up the stairs to the next floor
stairs-power-choices = Less than one horsepower
stairs-power-choices-2 = More than a horsepower: in short bursts a person is stronger than a horse
stairs-power-choices-3 = The same as walking: the stairs are the same — and so is the work
stairs-power-mass-label = Your mass
stairs-power-steps-label = Steps to the floor
stairs-power-rise-label = A step’s height
stairs-power-walk-label = Time walking
stairs-power-run-label = Time running
stairs-power-build-question = We measure ourselves. Stand on the floor scales, measure a step with a ruler and count the steps to the next floor. Then walk up one floor at an easy pace, and then run up — a friend times you each time with a stopwatch. (Under the scene are your measurements: an example for now, put in your own.) What power do you develop running up the stairs?
stairs-power-setup = Stairs to the next floor, floor scales, a ruler, a stopwatch — and a friend to time you
